\ Serial port 8250                                   clv 10dez00                                                                Tested on different ATs under volksForth 3.8.1. clv                                                                             This program handles the serial interface direct                via the 8250 chip registers (not via BIOS-calls!).              It doesn't check for paritiy or framing errors. This is fast.                                                                   It uses a 128 bytes queue to save the incoming bytes via        interrupt-routine. It could be more faster, if it uses          polling instead of interrupts. Try polling if you wan't to      use 115,200 baud ( the maximal possible baudrate of hardware )  but don't forget to buy the 33 MHz-AT with fast rams if you     wan't to enjoy the speed-up.                                    Author: Klaus Schleisick ( Hamburg West-Germany )               Changes: Claus.Vogt@Berlin.de  2000dec12: transmit              \ Serial port of 8250                                clv 13jun89                                                                Onlyforth \needs Assembler  2 loadfrom asm.scr                  include uti.scr  load: JCS .datim top? ;load                                       2  3 thru \ Variables and Queue                                 4  5 thru \ Interrupt routine                                   7  9 thru \ transmit & receive bytes                             &10 load \ optional stuff to handle 8250                    &13 &14 thru \ init & exit                        : bye    s_bye bye ;    s_cold                                \               &16 &18 thru \ Switch: baud com bits                            &19 &20 thru \ Receive&Transmit files           \               &22 &23 thru \ Terminal basroutines             \                   &24 load \ easy terminal                                                                                                                                                    \ Variables                                          clv 01jun89                                                                  Variable SINT      $c 4 * SINT !   \ abs. int-adress of COM1    Variable port      $3f8 port !     \ 8250 base adr   of COM1    : >port ( u -- adr ) port @ + ;                                 Variable baudMode  $180 baudMode ! \ 300 baud                   Variable bitMode   $07 bitMode !   \ 8+1 noParity +DTR +OUT2    Variable iLevel    $ef iLevel !    \ 8259 priority   of COM1    $20 >label I_ctrl                  \ Adresses of 8259 ..        $21 >label I_mask                  \ .. interrupt-controller                                                                    Create handshake \ all parameters for soft- and hardhandshake    Label soft?  Label softOff    0 c,  Label softOn       0 c,     Label last?  Label lastSend   0 c,  Label lastReceived 0 c,     Label hard?  Label txEmpty? $20 c,  Label txOk?      $30 c,                  Label hardOff  $1c c,  Label hardOn     $03 c,  \ queue                                              clv 13jun89                                                                  Defer 'tx   ' drop Is 'tx  \ used by TRANSMIT RECEIVE TERM      Defer 'rx   ' 0    Is 'rx                                                                                                       Create queue  0 , $80 allot                                                                                                   \\                                                                | 0   | 1   | 2                    | 130  byte address          | len | out |<-- 128 byte Queue -->|                                                                                            len ::= number of characters queued                             out ::= relative address of next output character               (len+out)mod(128) ::= relative address of first empty byte                                                                                                                                    \ s_int (interrupt service routine)               ks cîv 01jun89                                                                | Label end-ctrl  C: seg A- lastReceived #) mov                 | Label end-int                                                      $20 # A- mov   I_ctrl #) byte out          \ EOI for 8259       C pop  A pop   I pop   D pop   iret                                                                                        | Label putQueue  A- D+ mov    \ char in A-; changes D I A           Queue # I mov   C: seg I ) A mov   A- D- mov   D- inc           C: seg D- I ) mov   A+ A- add   $7F # A and   A I add           C: seg D+ 2 I D) mov   $68 # D- cmp  ret  end-code                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         \ s_int (interrupt service routine)               ks clv 08jun89| Label S_INT     D push   I push   A push  C push                   C: seg Port #) D mov   D byte in                                C: seg soft? #) C mov  C C or  0= not                           ?[ A- C- cmp  end-ctrl JE    A- C+ cmp  end-ctrl JE                putQueue # call     end-int JCS                                 C: seg lastSend #) C- cmp  end-int JE \ already OFF             C: seg  txempty? #) C+ mov                                      C: seg port #) D mov  5 # D add                                 [[ D byte in  C+ A- and  C+ A- cmp  0= ?]                       5 # D sub  C- A- mov  D byte out    \ OFF-char send             C: seg A- lastSend #) mov  end-int # jmp  ]?                 putQueue # call  end-int JCS                                    C: seg Port #) D mov  4 # D add  D byte in                      C: seg hardOff #) A- and   D byte out  \ -RTS -DTR              end-int # jmp  end-code                                    \\ s_int (interrupt service routine)               kscîv 01jun89                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                \ tx? tx                                          ks clv 08jun89                                                                  Code tx?  ( -- f )                                                 D push  C C xor  softOn #) A- mov  A- A- or                     0= ?[  Port #) D mov   5  # D add  D in                                hard? #) D mov  D A and  D A cmp                                0= ?[  C dec  ]?  \ true if transmitter empty & CTS            ][ lastReceived #) A- cmp  \ true if ON received..               0= ?[  Port #) D mov   5  # D add  D byte in                           txEmpty? #) D- mov  D- A- and D- A- cmp                         0= ?[ C dec ]? ]? ]? \ .. and transm. empty       C D mov  next  end-code                                                                                                      Code tx   ( c -- )   D- A- xchg   Port #) D mov                    D byte out   D pop   Next   end-code                                                                                       \ rx?                                             ks clv 08jun89                                                                  Code rx?  ( -- f )   D push   D D xor                              Queue #) D- mov   D- D- or  0=                                  ?[  [[  D push   Port #) D mov                                          softOn #) C- mov  C- C- or  0=                                  ?[  4 # D add  D byte in  \ +RTS +DTR                               hardOn #) A- or   D byte out                                 ][ lastSend #) C- cmp 0= not                                       ?[ txempty? #) C+ mov  5 # D add                                   [[ D byte in  C+ A- and  C+ A- cmp  0= ?]                       5 # D sub  C- A- mov  D byte out                                A- lastSend #) mov                                           ]?                                                          ]?  D pop                                          swap ]?  Next   end-code                                        \ rx                                                 clv 01jun89                                                                  Code rx   ( -- 8b )  I W mov   Queue # I mov                       D push   D D xor   cli   lods   A- A- or  0= not                ?[  A+ C- mov   A- dec   A+ inc   $7F # A+ and                      A -2 I D) mov   D- C+ mov   C I add   I ) D- mov            ]?  sti   W I mov   $18 # A- cmp  CS not ?]   Next           end-code      \ liefert 0 wenn kein Zeichen vorhanden                                                                         \ $02 = +RTS    $03 = +RTS+DTR                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  \ -dtr +dtr te?                                      clv 01jun89                                                                  Code -dtr    D push   Port #) D mov  4 # D add                     D byte in   $1E # A- and   D byte out   D pop   Next         end-code                                                                                                                        Code +dtr    D push   Port #) D mov  4 # D add                     D byte in   1 # A- or   D byte out   D pop   Next            end-code                                                                                                                        Code te?  ( -- f ) \ tests if transmitter is empty                 D push   Port #) D mov   5  # D add                             D in   D D xor   $0020 # A and   $0020 # A cmp                  0= ?[  D dec  ]?   Next   end-code                                                                                                                                                                                                              clv 11mai89                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                \\ Serial initialization - Assembler              ks clv 08jun89\ \\\ besser in High-Level :                                    | Code S_init  D push \ D: push   A A xor   A D: mov   C: A mov \    C: seg SINT #) W mov   S_INT # W ) mov   A 2 W D) mov      (     D: pop    )   Port #) D mov                                    3 # D add  \ $80 # A- mov   D byte out \ DLAB = 1               2 # D sub \  baudMode #) A mov   A- A+ xchg   D byte out        D dec  \ A- A+ xchg   D byte out                 \ baudrate     3 # D add  \ $907 # A mov   D out  \ 8bit, 1stop 0par                                             \ +DTR +OUT2             \      2 # D sub   1 # A- mov   D byte out             \ +rxINT Code xx D push     I_mask #) byte in   iLevel #) A- and              I_mask #) byte out                                            D pop   Next end-code    \  s_init t                                                                                                                                                         \  Serial initialization - High-Level                clv 08jun89  : s_init_interrupts                                                s_int  0 sint @    l!       \ Installs Interrupt-Offset- ..     ds@    0 sint @ 2+ l!       \ .. and Segment-Adress             $01  1 >port pc!            \ +rxInt                            i_mask pc@  iLevel @ and  i_mask pc! ; \ int.-control        : s_init                                                           $80  3 >port pc!            \ divisor Latch bit (DLAB) on..     ( baudMode @  port @  p! )  \ .. to set baud divisor            baudMode @  $100 u/mod 1 >port pc!  0 >port pc!                 bitmode @  3 >port pc!      \ parity/bits/stopbits/DLAB=0       $0b 4 >port pc!             \ +dtr +out2 +rts                   soft? @ IF softOn c@ dup lastSend c! lastReceived c!                     ELSE hardOn c@  4 >port under pc@ or swap pc! THEN     s_init_interrupts ;                                                                                                        \ s_cold s_bye s_exit sInts bye                      clv 11mai89                                                                | Create sInts  &16 allot       \ to save Interrupt-Vectors                                                                       : s_cold  0 $30  ds@ sInts  &16 lmove \ save Interrupt-Vectors            queue off  s_init ;                                                                                                   : s_exit  0 [ Port @ 1+ ] Literal  pc!    \ -rxINT                        0 [ Port @ 4 + ] Literal pc!    \ -dtr/-rts/-out2               I_mask pc@ iLevel @ not or I_mask pc! ;                                                                               : s_bye   ds@ sInts  0 $30   &16 lmove  s_exit ;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   clv 11mai89                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                \ baud COM1 COM2                                     clv 18mai89                                                                  : baud    ( d -- )                                                 IF drop 1 ELSE 115.200 rot 2 umax um/mod nip THEN               baudmode ! s_init ;                                                                                                        | : com: ( int# port iLev -- ) Create  not c,  ,  4 * c,             does> s_exit                                                     dup c@  iLevel !  1+ dup @ port !  2+ c@ SINT !                 s_init ;                                                                                                                    $c $3f8 $10 com: COM1                                           $b $2f8 $08 com: COM2                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         \ parity start/stop-Bits                             clv 18mai89                                                                | : par: ( u -- u+1 ) Create c,                                       does> c@  bitMode @  $c7 and or  bitMode !                      s_init ;                                                                                                                      $00 par: none        $38 par: low    $28 par: high              $18 par: even        $08 par: odd                                                                                           | : bit: ( u -- u+1 ) Create dup c, 1+                                does> c@  bitMode @  $07 not and or  bitMode !                  s_init ;                                                   0 bit: 5+1   bit: 6+1   bit: 7+1   bit: 8+1                       bit: 5+1.5 bit: 6+2   bit: 7+2   bit: 8+2 drop                                                                                                                                               \ XON/XOFF RTS/DTR RTS                               clv 01jun89                                                                  : Hs: ( hardOn-bm  tx-ok-bm txempty-bm on-char off-char -- )       Create c,  c,  0 c,  0 c,    c, c, dup not c, c,                does> handshake 8 cmove ;                                                                                                     $03 $30 $20       0       0   Hs: RTS/DTR                       $02 $10 $20       0       0   Hs: RTS                             0   0 $20  Ctrl q  Ctrl s   Hs: XON/XOFF                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   \ rtEnd rtAbort rtEof f@ f! ...                      clv 10dez00                                                                include uti.scr   load: stay ;load                              \needs 2Variable   : 2Variable Create 4 allot ;                    2Variable rtBytes  \ number of bytes send or received           : rtInit  0. rtBytes 2! ;                                       : rtEnd   ." --- " rtBytes 2@ d. ." bytes. " bell                         isfile@ [ dos ] fclose ;                              : rtEof   rtEnd ." END OF FILE ****" ;                          : rt?exit  key?                                                    IF key esc? IF rtEnd ." aborted ****" rdrop exit THEN              'tx THEN ; \ leaves calling word perhaps                  : +rtByte  output push display  stay                               rtBytes 2@  1. d+  2dup d.  rtBytes 2! ;                     : f@ ( -- c )  isfile@ [ dos ] fgetc +rtByte ;                  : f! ( c -- )  isfile@ [ dos ] fputc +rtByte ;               \ Receive Transmit                                   clv 10dez00                                                                \ receives file without changes until first EOF-Char. esc aborts  : Receive   ( | filename -- ) pushfile Makefile  rtInit           cr ." *** Receive:"  isfile @ [ dos ] .file                     BEGIN BEGIN rt?exit rx? 0= WHILE pause REPEAT                     rx  eof? IF #eof f! rtEof exit THEN f!                          REPEAT ;                                                  \ transmits file without changes. No EOF-Char appended. esc abor  : Transmit ( | filename -- ) pushfile Use  rtInit                 cr ." ***Transmit:" isfile @ [ dos ] .file .when ." --- "       BEGIN BEGIN  BEGIN rx? WHILE 'rx drop REPEAT                      rt?exit tx? 0= WHILE pause REPEAT                               f@ -1 case?  IF rtBytes 2@ -1. d+ rtBytes 2!                       rtEof exit THEN tx                                           BEGIN rx? WHILE 'rx drop REPEAT  REPEAT ;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \ ?rx ?key                                           clv 01jun89                                                                | : ?rx         pause rx? 0=exit rx                                  #LF case? IF  cr       exit    THEN                             #CR case? IF  Row 0 at exit    THEN                             #BS case? IF  del exit  THEN   emit ;                                                                                      | : ?key  ( -- c )   BEGIN ?rx key? UNTIL key ;                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 \ 'tx xwait txEcho txNoEcho                          clv 01jun89                                                                  : wTx BEGIN te? UNTIL tx ; \ PrÅft auf transmitter empty                                                                      | : txEcho ( c -- )                                                  #CR case? IF  cr  #CR wTx #LF wTx exit THEN                     #BS case? IF  del #BS wTx exit THEN  dup emit wtx ;                                                                        | : txNoEcho ( c -- )                                                #CR case? IF #CR wTx #LF THEN wTx ;                                                                                          : halfduplex ['] txEcho Is 'tx ;  halfduplex                    : fullduplex ['] txNoEcho Is 'tx ;                                                                                                                                                                                                                            \ term termcold - easy terminal program              clv 06jun89                                                                  : term                                                             ." Terminal:" "datim" count type ." - Type <esc> to leave"      cr  status off .status                                          BEGIN ?key  #esc case?                                             IF ." TERM to reenter - BYE to quit" cr                            status on .status  quit THEN                                'tx REPEAT ;                                             \\                                                              | : termcold     s_cold                                              interpret  page  term  ( bye ) ;                                                                                           ' termcold Is 'cold                                             \ savesystem TERM.COM                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           \\ A brief 8250-description                          clv 11mai89                                                                General note: xF8 and xF9 emulate different registers                             dependant of the DLAB (divisor Latch bit)       register xF9,xFB can be read. All other write only                                                                            xF8,xF9 : IF DLAB=1 : divisor latch for baudrate                    the baudRate is 115200/dla so possible rates: 2..115200 baudxF8     : IF DLAB=0 and WRITE: transmit buffer                  xF8     : IF DLAB=0 and READ : receive buffer                   xF9     : IF DLAB=0 : interrupt enable register                 xFA     : interrupt identification register                     xFB     : line control register                                 xFC     : modem control register                                xFD     : line status register                                  xFE     : modem status register                                 \\                                                   clv 11mai89                                                                interrupt enable: enables interrupt on condition: (4..7==0)     bit 0: byte received                                                1: transmitter empty, give me more to transmit (3..7==0)        2: line-status: framing-, parity-, overrun-error or break       3: modem-status: change on an handshake-line                                                                                interrupt identification: it there an interrupd an why?             0: there is no interrupt if set                              1..2: interrupt type (in descending order of priority)               =11 line-status                                                 =10 byte received                                               =01 transmitter empty                                           =00 modem-status                                                                                                          \\                                                   clv 18mai89                                                                line control register (may be read also)                         0..2: controls number of bits and stopbits.                     3..5: controls parity-modes.                                       6: break control bit. forces SOUT to logical 0 state            7: divisor-latch-bit. To access divisor Latch.                                                                              modem control:                                                      0: sets DTR (Data-Terminnal-Ready)                              1: sets RTS (Request-To-Send)                                   2: sets OUT1                                                    3: sets OUT2                                                    4: diagnostic (connects inputs with outputs,                                   so that the outer world is isolated                             and the 8250 talks to itself)                \\                                                   clv 11mai89                                                                line status:    ( 7==0)                                             0: Data Ready , resets when you read byte received              1: overrun error, you didn't read the byte before next          3: framin error, no valid stop-bit detected                     4: break interrupt, 0-state received for long time              5: transmitter empty, give me more                                                                                          modem status:   (0..3 generates interrupts)                         0: CTS changed              4: CTS                              1: DSR changed              5: DSR                              2: RI  changed to inactive  6: RI                               3: DCD changed              7: DCD                                                                                                                                                          \\ S_INT                                             clv 01jun89                                                                S_INT will be installed bye s_init as RS232-Service-Interrupt      Doesn't check, if the interrupt was generated because           of received byte.                                               Reads the received byte and puts it into the queue.             If the queue is nearly full, changes handshake.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                end-code                                                      \ $1c = -RTS-DTR  $1d = -RTS                                    \\ s_int (interrupt service routine)               ksclv 01jun89S_INT works internally like this:                                    save registers;                                                 DX:=portadr;   AL:=received char;  CX:=handshake-chars;         IF any handshake-char specified                                 {  IF AL==handshake-char { remember AL; TERMINATE; }               put char into QUEUE; IF queue not full {TERMINATE;}             CH:=transmitter-empty-bitmask                                   DX:=line-status-register-adress                                 REPEAT { AL:=line-status } UNTIL transmitter empty              DX:=transmitter-register; putOut CL==waitChar;                  TERMINATE;                                                   }ELSE{ put char into QUEUE; IF queue not full {TERMINATE;}         DX:=modem-control-register;                                     AL:=bitmask-for-wait-state; set lines to wait-state;            TERMINATE }                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             \\ tx? tx                                            clv 01jun89                                                                TX?  checks if transmitter holding register is empty                 and if handshake says that a byte can be transmitted                                                                       TX   transmits byte without any check.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          \\ rx?                                               clv 06jun89                                                                RX? checks if there is a byte received                              by checking if the queue is not empty                           changes handshake if the queue is nearly empty                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              \\ rx                                                clv 06jun89                                                                RX  gets a byte received. gets 0 if there is none.                  changes handshake if the queue is nearly empty                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              \\ +dtr -dtr                                         clv 06jun89                                                                -DTR sets the Data-Terminal-Ready-Line to logical high          +DTR sets the Data-Terminal-Ready-Line to logical low                                                                           TE?  tests if the transmitter-register of the 8250 is empty.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    \\  Serial initialization - High-Level               clv 06jun89                                                                S_INIT restarts the Chip. Prior to it, S_COLD must be                  executed. All words that change paramters                       of the v24 should execute it to tell the Chip                   the changed parameters.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  \\ s_cold s_bye s_exit sInts bye                     clv 06jun89                                                                SINTS these 16 bytes are used to save the old rs232-Interrupt-        Vectors                                                                                                                   S_COLD initializes the rs232 for the first time.                      saves the old interrupt-vectors, empties the QUEUE              and executes S_INIT.                                      S_EXIT exits the rs232 by switching the interrupt off.                Used especially by COM1 and COM2 prior to using                 S_INIT with the new rs232-Line                                                                                            S_BYE resets the rs232 by reinstalling the old interrupt-vectors      and executing S_EXIT. Attention! No parameters are              reset to their initial state (before S_COLD) because            most of these parameters cannot be read.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  \\                                                   clv 18mai89                                                                BAUD ( d -- )                                                     Setzt die baudrate auf d.                                       Hierzu wird der entsprechende Teiler (115200/d) in BAUDMODE     gesetzt und die Schnittstelle neu erîfnet. (S_INIT)                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           COM1 und COM2                                                     schalten auf den ersten bzw. zweiten seriellen Port des PC.     Hierzu setzen sie den derzeitigen Port zurÅck (S_EXIT),         verÑndern die PORT-adresse und die zugehîrigen Parameter        des Interruptcontrollers und îffnen den neuen Port (S_INIT)   \\ parity start/stop-Bits                            clv 06jun89                                                                NONE LOW HIGH EVEN ODD                                             set the parity to the specified mode.                                                                                        5+1 5+1.5 6+1 6+2 7+1 7+2 8+1 8+2                                  set the Number of bits and stop-bits to the specified number.   (for example: 6+2 sets 6 bits and 2 stop-bits                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                \\ XON/XOFF RTS/DTR RTS                              clv 01jun89                                                                XON/XOFF RTS/DTR RTS                                              Either of these sets handshake for subsequent data-transfers.   Don't forget: The other side must use the same protocol!                                                                      XON/XOFF uses chars Ctrl-s  / Ctrl-q to force the sender            to wait / continue. Most devices that want to spare cables      use XON/XOFF-protocol                                                                                                       RTS/DTR  sets both RTS- and DTR-line  to low/high pegel             to force the sender to wait / continue.                         This hardware-handshake is the safety method. Most devices      understand it properly. Don't use with acousic couplers.        cause they will lay down.                                   RTS sets RTS-line to low/high to wait/continue.                 \\ rtEnd rtAbort rtEof f@ f! ...                     clv 06jun89                                                                internal words for RECEIVE and TRANSMIT                                                                                         RTEND RTABORT closes the file and outputs number of bytes.                                                                      F@ F!  gets/puts a char from/to file. outputs number of bytes                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   \\ Receive Transmit                                  clv 06jun89                                                                RECEIVE receives chars from rs232 and writes them to the           specified file.                                                 If an EOF-Char is detected, it is also                          written to the file and RECEIVE terminates.                     You can interrupt it by typing <Esc>.                           The number of bytes received is  output consecutively.                                                                       TRANSMIT transmits all chars from the specified file to rs232      without any change.                                             You can interrupt it by typing <Esc>.                           The number of bytes received is  output consecutively.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       \\ ?rx ?key                                          clv 06jun89                                                                internal words for TERM                                                                                                         ?RX receives a char from rs232 and puts it out if any.              Carriage Return, Line Feed and Backspace are treated correct                                                                ?KEY executes ?RX until a console-key is pressed and returns key                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                \\ 'tx xwait txEcho txNoEcho                         clv 06jun89                                                                WTX transmits a char to rs232 when the transmitter-register         ist empty. Doesn't check handshake.                                                                                         TXECHO transmits a char to rs232 (per WTX). doesn't check hands.    Carriage Return will transmit both: CR and Line Feed            All characters are echoed to the display                    TXNOECHO                                                            transmits a char to rs232 (per WTX). doesn't check handshak.    Carriage Return will transmit both: CR and Line Feed.           Nothing is echoed to the display                                                                                            HALFDUPLEX / FULLDUPLEX switches Echo-Mode by installing            TXECHO / TXNOECHO as 'TX.                                                                                                   \\ term termcold - easy terminal program             clv 06jun89                                                                TERM transmits keys from the console to the rs232 and vice versa   thus emulating a terminal. Can be left by typing <esc>.         Use S_COLD once before using TERM.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           TERMCOLD may be used as 'COLD to make a stand-alone-system.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     